pull_request.body:
This PR replaces the single-neighbor framing with a criteria-based literature position.

Article changes:
- removes the implication that Workspace Optimization is the overall nearest precedent;
- separates the structural lineage from computational reflection, Models@run.time, requirements reflection, and architecture-based self-adaptation;
- separates the epistemic lineage from explanation-based learning and empirical theory refinement;
- states the proposed contribution as their conjunction in one longitudinal self-modification path;
- retains Workspace Optimization as a close contemporary LLM-agent implementation analogue;
- keeps the recent harnesses as nearby fragments rather than the defining comparison.

New durable note:
- explains why “closest” requires a named comparison axis;
- distinguishes object/target, learning mechanism, and implementation morphology;
- records the limitations of each lineage;
- states the proposed synthesis without claiming it has already been demonstrated;
- derives stronger experimental baselines: runtime self-modeling/self-adaptation, explicit theory refinement, Workspace Optimization, and direct or parametric alternatives.

The article remains compact; the detailed source positioning and primary-source links live in `theory-mediated-system-learning-combines-runtime-self-modeling-with-theory-refinement.md`.
